WEBVTT

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:03.250
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.420
Attack Decode Talker!

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:09.090
Ultimate Malicious Code!

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.970
Topologic Bomber Dragon's 
terror is only starting!

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.690
Topologic Bomber Dragon's effect activates.

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:29.610
After attacking your monster, you take 
damage equal to your monster's original ATK!

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:30.840
What?

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.840
2300 damage!

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.310
You lose, Playmaker!

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:37.550
Aiming Blast!

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:57.770
I run Across the universe

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:00.940
At the speed of light

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:02.810
Begin Loading

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:06.540
Open the door of dreams

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:10.110
VRAINS spreads

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:13.220
Believe in myself

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:16.750
VRAINS continues

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:22.060
The circuit draws the future

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:26.130
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:27.730
Access!

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:30.430
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:32.040
I'm now With the Wind

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:34.340
Link with my soul

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:37.110
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.840
Now Win the Race

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:41.680
Connected world

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:45.180
No matter when

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:48.550
Nothing is impossible

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:52.690
Strive for hope

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:57.260
And ride the wind!

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.950
Yusaku, do something!

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.190
Playmaker is going to lose.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:21.790
I activate the Counter Trap, Link Restart!

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.870
When a card effect that deals me damage 
activates, that activation is negated!

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:33.820
Then I banish this card from my graveyard...

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:36.690
...to Special Summon a Link 
Monster from my graveyard!

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.670
Resurrect, Decode Talker!

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:47.920
You avoided Topologic Bomber 
and improved your situation.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:49.450
You're quite tough.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:52.220
I end my turn.

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:57.190
So the Continuous Spell Dragonoid 
Generator's effect activates.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:03.900
You must Special Summon one Dragonoid 
Token in attack position on your field.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:08.850
In that case, I Special 
Summon a Dragonoid Token.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:14.270
My turn!  I draw!

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:16.010
This is bad.

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:21.010
We managed to survive, but we'll lose 
if we don't do something this turn.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:22.400
I know.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:25.300
We'll have to execute our special plan.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:30.320
There's only one way we can win.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:32.660
Storm Access.

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:34.240
Exactly!

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:38.620
And we need to get a monster 
that's stronger than his.

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:41.700
So we'll need a bigger Data Storm.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.470
You want me to pray for that to happen?

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:49.110
AIs don't pray.  We only 
calculate ways to win!

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:57.840
Releasing Cyberse data material!

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:12.770
What's this?

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:16.330
This also happened when 
I first saw Playmaker.

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:21.620
I knew you'd do it.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:24.050
I was waiting for this moment.

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:27.280
My goal for this Speed Duel is now complete.

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:30.000
Seems we're now ready.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.020
Having to destroy your own child...

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:36.240
So this is poetic justice.

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:44.560
Father, seems you're ready.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:51.470
Go, Playmaker!

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:54.680
Your courage will give rise to a new power!

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:56.410
Activate Skill!

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:04.850
When I have 1000 or lower LP, I get one 
random Link Monster in the Data Storm!

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:08.610
It's a giant Data Storm!

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:12.330
There's definitely someone powerful in here!

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:28.620
Now!  Seize the wind, Playmaker!

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:31.020
Storm Access!

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:37.680
I'm impressed.

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:40.440
This is the key card for a comeback!

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.620
Appear!

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:44.110
The circuit that leads to the future!

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:49.560
Sorry, but I won't let you use that card.

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:52.660
I activate the trap, Remote Rebirth!

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:55.400
What?

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:57.640
A trap at this moment?

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:04.740
It Special Summons a monster from your 
graveyard next to Topologic Bomber Dragon's link.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:05.710
No way!

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:09.110
Resurrect, Capacitor Stalker!

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:12.020
Unbelievable!  If you do this-

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:13.380
I know.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:17.260
Topologic Bomber Dragon's 
effect now activates.

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:20.570
When a monster is Special 
Summoned next to its link...

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:24.500
...all monsters in our Main 
Monster Zones are destroyed.

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:26.400
Full Overlap!

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:40.180
When Capacitor Stalker is destroyed, 
its effect deals us both 800 damage.

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:46.770
Trying to escape with a tie?

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:48.620
No, that's not my intention.

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:52.090
I can anticipate all your moves!

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.220
W-What's this?

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:03.940
I used your power to my advantage.

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:06.410
So you planned for all this?

00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:07.770
Exactly.

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:12.710
A Speed Duel is too limiting for our fight.

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:15.950
The next stage is waiting for us.

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:19.220
W-What's going on?

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:20.690
Yusaku!

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:31.530
What happened to them?

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:33.730
The tornado swallowed them up!

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:36.070
Go after them, Ghost Girl!

00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:39.070
Don't be crazy!  I can't see anything!

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:44.810
Aoi...

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:53.960
They're planning to finish this 
where we can't reach them.

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:57.880
If Ignis falls into Knights 
of Hanoi' hands...

00:07:57.880 --> 00:08:00.990
...that'll put our company 
in the worst situation.

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:08.970
We should be more worried about why the 
Knights of Hanoi can control the Data Storm.

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:13.480
The one who can do this is...  It can't be...

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:35.350
It's the center of the 
Data Storm.  It's quiet.

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:41.930
This is his field.

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:47.130
You arrived, Playmaker.

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:50.740
This is the scene for our new battle.

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:02.590
We will settle this in a Master Duel.

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:04.560
Master Duel...

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:11.530
In a Master Duel, the Monster Zone and Spell 
& Trap Zones are bigger than in a Speed Duel.

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:18.600
The true power of a Link Monster's Link 
Markers can only be unleashed in a Master Duel.

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:23.370
Now you and I can fully use our powers.

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:26.610
Fine.  I will finish you here.

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:35.240
What's that card?

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:38.170
A card to power up his Master Duel.

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:43.090
It's true that Speed Duel and Master Duel 
strategies are completely different.

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:44.690
Let's do this.

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:47.330
Duel!

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:58.690
No good!  I can't get in!

00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:01.650
Damn.  What's happening inside?

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:04.390
I'll go first.

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:08.470
I activate the Field Spell, Fire Prison.

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:22.670
As long as I have this card, 
Dragons on my field gain 300 DEF.

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:27.220
And if we want to summon a Link Monster...

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:32.690
...its Link Number must be equal or more 
than the highest monster on the field.

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:36.650
Only Link Monsters can attack.

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:41.220
And this card can't be destroyed 
by other cards' effects!

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:43.080
Fire Prison...

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:45.710
Is that the card he just got?

00:10:45.710 --> 00:10:49.450
Limiting links is going to be a problem!

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:53.230
I sense an eerie power that's even worse.

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:57.770
I summon Sniffer Dragon.

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:03.740
Sniffer Dragon's effect activates.

00:11:03.740 --> 00:11:07.210
When this card is Normal 
or Special Summoned...

00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:11.460
...I can add one Sniffer 
Dragon in my deck to my hand.

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:15.170
Next, I activate the Quick-Play 
Spell, Quick Revolve!

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:20.130
I Special Summon one Varret 
monster from my deck.

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:23.080
Appear, Magnavarrett Dragon!

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:27.700
Huh?  He's never used that monster before.

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:30.670
He's using his real deck.

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:34.520
Appear!  The future circuit 
that lights up my path!

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:43.880
Arrowheads confirmed.

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:48.900
The summoning conditions are 
two Level 4 or lower Dragons.

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:54.540
I set Sniffer Dragon and Magnavarrett 
Dragon in the Link Markers!

00:11:56.720 --> 00:11:58.630
Circuit combine!

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:06.900
Link Summon!

00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:11.580
Appear, Link 2 Twin Triangle Dragon!

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:21.400
I Special Summon Beltlink 
Wall Dragon from my hand!

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:27.160
In defense position?

00:12:27.420 --> 00:12:35.130
I can Special Summon it when a Dragon-Type 
Link Monster is summoned to my field.

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:41.210
When this card is Special Summoned, 
it gets two Wall Counters.

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:47.210
Neither of us can summon a Link Monster 
that's higher than the number of Wall Counters.

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:50.980
And only Link Monsters can attack!

00:12:50.980 --> 00:12:52.880
That's not all.

00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:56.920
Due to Fire Prison's effect, it gains DEF!

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:59.060
2400 DEF...

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:01.740
What's wrong, Playmaker?

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:05.620
I didn't expect him to 
strengthen his defenses.

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:08.670
His play style is more 
cautious than we thought.

00:13:09.340 --> 00:13:12.640
Or maybe it's part of his plan.

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:15.370
I end my turn.

00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:18.110
My turn!  I draw!

00:13:18.510 --> 00:13:21.060
Beltlink Wall Dragon's effect!

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:24.080
It gains a Wall Counter 
during each of our turns!

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:28.960
It was careless to let him to go first.

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:31.850
Due to Fire Prison and 
Beltlink Wall Dragon...

00:13:31.850 --> 00:13:35.200
...he has the advantage in 
summoning Link Monsters.

00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:39.660
Only Link 2 and 3 Link Monsters 
can currently be summoned.

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:42.510
I Special Summon Linkslayer!

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:49.770
I can Special Summon this card from my 
hand when I have no monsters on my field.

00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:55.980
Nice!  Linkslayer has more ATK 
than Twin Triangle Dragon!

00:13:56.200 --> 00:14:02.190
But due to Beltlink Wall Dragon's 
effect, only Link Monsters can attack.

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:04.290
Oh yeah!  I forgot!

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:09.990
And Fire Prison can't be destroyed 
by other cards' effects.

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:12.970
Therefore, Linkslayer's effect is useless.

00:14:12.970 --> 00:14:16.570
I Special Summon Backup Secretary!

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:23.570
I can Special Summon this card from my 
hand when there's a Cyberse on the field.

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:26.440
Next, I summon Stack Reviver!

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:32.070
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:37.490
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:14:37.490 --> 00:14:41.330
The summoning conditions 
are at least two Cyberses!

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:47.710
I set Backup Secretary, Linkslayer and 
Stack Reviver in the Link Markers!

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:52.970
Circuit combine!

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:56.910
Link Summon!

00:14:56.910 --> 00:15:00.860
Appear, Link 3 Encode Talker!

00:15:06.060 --> 00:15:07.790
So you already summoned it.

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:11.140
I activate Stack Reviver's 
effect from my graveyard!

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:13.310
When this card is used to Link Summon...

00:15:13.310 --> 00:15:17.920
...I can Special Summon a Level 4 
or lower Cyberse from the graveyard.

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:21.430
Resurrect, Backup Secretary!

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:30.010
Battle!  Encode Talker attacks 
Twin Triangle Dragon!

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:32.060
That's not possible.

00:15:32.060 --> 00:15:33.010
What?

00:15:33.010 --> 00:15:35.380
Beltlink Wall Dragon's effect!

00:15:35.380 --> 00:15:39.480
Your Link Monster is only 
allowed to attack this card!

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:50.900
But I now Special Summon Interrupt 
Resistor from my hand!

00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:59.050
This card's ATK is equal to 
the damage I took in battle.

00:15:59.050 --> 00:16:01.700
You took 100 points of damage.

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:04.720
You summoned a monster with such low ATK?

00:16:05.640 --> 00:16:08.480
For real, right?  But 
it's in defense position.

00:16:09.350 --> 00:16:12.080
Playmaker's battle is over.

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:17.080
And by bringing out this card, 
there's another card he can use.

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:21.330
From my hand, I activate the 
spell card, Cyberse Cache!

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:25.970
When there's a Cyberse on my field whose 
ATK is different than its original ATK...

00:16:25.970 --> 00:16:28.030
...I draw two cards!

00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:32.400
Playmaker not only strengthened his 
defenses, he also drew two cards!

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:34.640
I see.

00:16:34.980 --> 00:16:38.540
I set one card and end my turn!

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:42.450
He knew he couldn't get past 
Beltlink Wall Dragon...

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:45.350
...so he prepared for a new Link Summon.

00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:49.280
But this strategy will cost you your life.

00:16:49.280 --> 00:16:51.820
The time for your destiny is near.

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:54.580
My turn!  I draw!

00:16:55.690 --> 00:16:58.000
Beltlink Wall Dragon's effect!

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:00.230
I place one Wall Counter.

00:17:00.230 --> 00:17:03.200
I summon Autovarrett Dragon!

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:09.810
Appear!  The future circuit 
that lights up my path!

00:17:11.980 --> 00:17:14.550
He's Link Summoning again!

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:17.880
And he's allowed to summon Link 4 monsters!

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:20.580
That means he can...  No way!

00:17:22.550 --> 00:17:24.890
Topologic Bomber Dragon!

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:28.080
If he uses Full Overlap, we're in trouble!

00:17:28.800 --> 00:17:30.590
Arrowheads confirmed.

00:17:30.840 --> 00:17:34.010
The summoning conditions 
are at least two monsters.

00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:40.570
I set Link 2 Twin Triangle Dragon and 
Autovarrett Dragon in the Link Markers!

00:17:42.430 --> 00:17:44.250
Circuit combine!

00:17:45.450 --> 00:17:47.050
Link Summon!

00:17:47.050 --> 00:17:51.470
Appear, Link 3 Three Burst Blast Dragon!

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:01.960
Beltlink Wall Dragon's effect!

00:18:02.460 --> 00:18:08.070
By Link Summoning a Dragon whose Link is 
less than the number of Wall Counters...

00:18:08.070 --> 00:18:11.010
...two Wall Counters are removed.

00:18:12.170 --> 00:18:14.410
Huh?  He didn't summon Topologic?

00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:19.880
Battle!  Three Burst Blast Dragon 
attacks Backup Secretary!

00:18:23.020 --> 00:18:25.190
He's not attacking Encode?

00:18:25.190 --> 00:18:29.100
Encode Talker's effect activates!

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:35.200
When the linked Backup Secretary 
battles a monster with higher ATK...

00:18:35.200 --> 00:18:38.670
...damage becomes 0, and she's 
not destroyed in battle!

00:18:38.670 --> 00:18:39.950
Not good enough!

00:18:39.950 --> 00:18:42.820
Three Burst Blast Dragon's effect!

00:18:42.820 --> 00:18:49.320
When this card battles, it can negate 
your spell, trap or effect once!

00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:52.830
But that effect can only 
be used once per turn!

00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:53.640
I...

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:56.380
Interrupt Resistor's effect!

00:18:56.380 --> 00:19:00.640
My defending monster's DEF becomes 
the same as Interrupt's...

00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:04.080
...and battle destruction is negated!

00:19:04.090 --> 00:19:08.240
But Three Burst Blast Dragon 
can deal piercing damage!

00:19:08.820 --> 00:19:12.920
The amount that exceeds her 
DEF is dealt to you as damage.

00:19:13.160 --> 00:19:14.400
Precision Lane!

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:23.770
I end my turn.

00:19:23.770 --> 00:19:29.250
Backup Secretary's DEF now returns to normal.

00:19:29.460 --> 00:19:31.700
What's his strategy?

00:19:31.700 --> 00:19:34.360
Why didn't he bring out Topologic?

00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:36.820
He might have a different goal.

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:40.980
Since he didn't use Topologic, he 
still has monsters on his field.

00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:43.900
And he'll use them to 
bring out a new monster!

00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:45.330
That's scary.

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:48.630
It's your turn, Playmaker.

00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:51.370
My turn!  I draw!

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:54.100
Beltlink's effect now activates!

00:19:54.110 --> 00:19:56.340
I place one Wall Counter.

00:19:56.580 --> 00:19:58.420
Beltlink is in the way!

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:00.520
It's protecting him!

00:20:00.520 --> 00:20:01.480
I know.

00:20:01.480 --> 00:20:03.380
I'll go for it this turn.

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:05.580
I summon Balancer Lord!

00:20:08.820 --> 00:20:11.790
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:19.520
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:20:19.520 --> 00:20:25.850
I set Balancer Lord, Interrupt Resistor 
and Backup Secretary in the Link Markers!

00:20:29.400 --> 00:20:31.260
Circuit combine!

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:34.310
Link Summon!

00:20:34.310 --> 00:20:38.370
Appear, Link 3 Decode Talker!

00:20:40.860 --> 00:20:47.040
Decode Talker gains 500 ATK for 
every monster that's linked to it!

00:20:47.690 --> 00:20:49.370
Power Integration!

00:20:53.360 --> 00:20:58.300
Now Decode Talker's ATK is 
higher than Beltlink's DEF!

00:20:58.300 --> 00:20:59.850
Are you sure?

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:03.370
I was waiting for this moment!

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:07.010
The Field Spell Fire 
Prison's effect activates!

00:21:12.720 --> 00:21:13.820
What?

00:21:14.240 --> 00:21:18.160
Cyberses in the field, graveyard and hand...

00:21:18.160 --> 00:21:21.360
...lose their effects and can't attack!

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:26.830
Cyberses also can't be targeted 
by effects nor attacked!

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:29.800
It's as if Cyberses don't exist!

00:21:36.580 --> 00:21:38.840
Cyberses are vanishing!

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:41.210
Playmaker!

00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:50.440
My senses are...  It's getting dark...

00:21:51.920 --> 00:21:53.160
Ai...

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:55.030
Vanish, Cyberse!

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:00.880
Ai...

00:22:24.000 --> 00:22:27.040
Dance!  Strike with your heels

00:22:27.270 --> 00:22:30.550
Scream!  You Gotta Go  Raise your voice

00:22:30.970 --> 00:22:34.180
Sing!  Unleash your existence

00:22:34.470 --> 00:22:38.220
Get Away!  Until you surpass your limits

00:22:40.110 --> 00:22:42.110
Try It over and over

00:22:43.850 --> 00:22:50.270
In this world that spreads forever

00:22:50.620 --> 00:22:57.210
The timeline flows forever

00:22:57.500 --> 00:22:59.770
Nothing is certain

00:22:59.900 --> 00:23:01.450
In these isolated times

00:23:01.740 --> 00:23:03.210
Set Yourself Free without hesitation

00:23:03.440 --> 00:23:04.980
Cuz We Still Believin' Magic

00:23:05.210 --> 00:23:08.380
The traces we leave behind

00:23:08.510 --> 00:23:11.950
The traces we leave behind

00:23:12.150 --> 00:23:15.920
The miracles we create

00:23:16.180 --> 00:23:18.160
Never Give Up Never!

00:23:18.160 --> 00:23:21.970
I won't give up  Never Give Up Never!

00:23:36.910 --> 00:23:41.020
The electric flower blooms, 
and Cyberse vanishes.

00:23:41.020 --> 00:23:44.520
But Revolver doesn't stop attacking.

00:23:44.520 --> 00:23:51.380
The brightness of his enemy's future 
circuit leads Playmaker to a harsher fate.

00:23:51.600 --> 00:23:54.100
Cyberse is still here.

00:23:54.100 --> 00:23:56.580
I can hear their pulse!

00:23:57.130 --> 00:24:01.740
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Roar of the Magazine  Varreload

00:24:01.740 --> 00:24:04.320
Into the VRAINS!
